  "notes": "Own site (govisitchins.com, redirects to www) links to a current dated dine-in menu PDF (filename dated 2026_0722). pdftotext -layout produced clean, confidently-paired name/price text (only 2 pages, mostly single-item-per-line tables), cross-checked against the visual layout description in the text. Entrees are priced by protein category (Chicken/Shrimp/Pork/Fish/Scallops/Beef/Vegetables & Tofu) with separate Lunch and Dinner prices for every dish in that category - both were captured as separate dish rows (section suffixed Lunch/Dinner) per the several-distinct-menus rule, since this restaurant genuinely runs two price tiers all day rather than one. A House Specialties section had 5 dishes with prices distinct from the base category pricing (kept) and several duplicate listings of dishes already priced elsewhere in the PDF (skipped to avoid double counting) - one specialty (Pao Hu Pork) showed only a single price with no visible lunch/dinner split, recorded as-is and noted. Fried Rice and Lo Mein are build-your-own base dishes priced by size (small/large) rather than lunch/dinner; captured that way. No drink/bar menu found on the site - this is a Chinese dine-in restaurant that does not appear to publish a separate bar list; Beverage is a flat .95 line item on the food menu itself.",
